# Answer key for B3 t5_metamorphic.sql - pairs and one realistic job.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE.
# P1-P5 must be equal: facts listed once, at spelling A. P6 is a SEAM pair: the key holds
# both spellings' facts and says which owns which. Conventions: B1/B2 plus D-15..D-18.

@ 22 P1 ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE vs MERGE
value fct_order_line.order_date -> sales_daily.sale_date identity
value fct_order_line.store_id -> sales_daily.store_id identity
value fct_order_line.gross_amount -> sales_daily.gross_amount aggregated
influence fct_order_line.order_date, fct_order_line.store_id -> sales_daily.gross_amount
forbid filter fct_order_line.store_id -> sales_daily | the conflict target (A) and the MERGE ON (B) are both structural (D-15, D-5)

@ 47 P2 CTE-fed INSERT vs inlined
value payments.order_id -> top_customers.customer_id identity
value payments.amount -> top_customers.revenue identity
filter payments.method -> top_customers

@ 66 P3 omitted vs explicit column list
value dim_store.region -> kpi_rollup.region identity
value dim_store.country_code -> kpi_rollup.country_code identity
filter dim_store.status -> kpi_rollup

@ 82 P4 SET a = x, b = y vs SET (a, b) = (x, y)
value dim_warehouse.name -> dim_warehouse.name derived
value dim_warehouse.capacity -> dim_warehouse.capacity derived
filter dim_warehouse.status -> dim_warehouse

@ 96 P5 DELETE ... IN vs EXISTS
filter returns.order_line_id, order_lines.id, order_lines.status -> returns

@ 115 P6 SEAM DELETE ... USING vs EXISTS
filter orders.status -> payments
@ 121 P6 B (spelling B's own facts, at its line - B4-04)
filter orders.id, payments.order_id -> payments
note Spelling B only: the EXISTS correlation's operands. In A, `o.id = p.order_id` joins USING to the target (D-11) - the semi-join seam left open in B2.

@ 141 R1 the nightly customer job
value orders.customer_id -> customer_summary.customer_id identity
value orders.order_ts -> customer_summary.first_order_date, customer_summary.last_order_date, customer_summary.status aggregated
value customer_summary.lifetime_orders -> customer_summary.lifetime_orders derived
note The accumulator `cs.lifetime_orders + EXCLUDED.lifetime_orders`; the inserted count is COUNT(*), which has no source.
value orders.amount, payments.amount -> customer_summary.lifetime_value aggregated
value payments.status, payments.paid_at -> customer_summary.lifetime_value aggregated
note D-14: the archived refunds reach the summary only through a LEFT JOIN, so their predicate decides lifetime_value and removes no summary row.
influence orders.customer_id -> customer_summary.first_order_date, customer_summary.last_order_date, customer_summary.lifetime_orders, customer_summary.lifetime_value, customer_summary.status
filter orders.status, customer_summary.status -> customer_summary
filter payments.status, payments.paid_at -> payments
note The DELETE in `archived` removes those payments (convention (c)).
forbid filter payments.status -> customer_summary | reaches the summary only through a LEFT JOIN: it cannot remove a summary row (D-14)
